{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Elohim called the dry land Earth.</b> He says that its proper name is \"dry land,\" for when the waters separated from the dust it is dry, but He calls it \"earth\" like the name of the totality of the elements created first. The reason is that for its sake they were created — that it be a habitation for man, for among the lower beings none recognizes its Creator except it. And He called the gathering of the waters \"seas,\" as though it were \"a sea of waters,\" because the floor of the gathering is called \"sea,\" as it is written (Isaiah 11:9), \"as the waters cover the sea,\" and likewise \"and the sea he removed from upon the cattle\" (II Kings 16:17) — because since it is a gathering of much water it is called so." "<b>And Elohim saw that it was good.</b> This is their endurance by His will, and the matter is that when He clothed them with this form He desired them, and the endurance was as I have explained (Ramban on Genesis 1:4). And this is what our Rabbis said (Genesis Rabbah 4:6): Why was \"that it was good\" not said on the second day? Because the work of the waters was not completed; therefore it is written on the third day two times — one for the work of the waters and one for the work of the day."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase שֶׁאֵין בַּתַּחְתּוֹנִים מַכִּיר בּוֹרְאוֹ זוּלָתוֹ literally says 'among the lower beings none recognizes its Creator except it'; the masculine suffix in זוּלָתוֹ appears to refer back to אֶרֶץ, though the grammar is slightly strained."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-21T22:13:12.241560306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}